+                            <p>Elevation matters too. Homes on the higher foothill streets toward Butterfield Canyon catch more wind and snow than homes down near Redwood Road. Wind pushes on wide doors, ice builds up at the threshold, and cold mornings put extra strain on worn springs. A door that was merely noisy in October can be the one that won&#x27;t open in January.</p>
